{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"5f49461d431c8d05b3c9c8cfb8c9ed47dcb6f2a41612c33fbf9dfe14a0bdb18c","digest":{"component_or_area":"gerrit-verify CI gate / test infrastructure","key_entities":["gerrit-verify.yaml","test.yml","pytest-xdist","setup-python","docs/coverage.md","build-and-test step","--durations","fail_under = 70"],"problem_keywords":["ci performance","test parallelization","pytest-xdist","pip caching","build time","gerrit verify gate","coverage","test durations"],"propositions":["The gerrit-verify gate's build-and-test phase has a critical path of 32–42 minutes; serial pytest execution on 5,701 tests takes ~1361s, blocking the Verified gate.","pytest-xdist parallelization with -n4 --dist worksteal reduces test wall-clock from 1361s to 331s (5× speedup) with identical outcomes and only 6% coverage overhead.","No pip cache exists in any CI workflow; install time for the heavy dev + agents dependency stack is rebuilt cold every job (19s cold vs 9s warm).","The gate must log per-test durations (--durations) and store them to support performance regression detection.","Coverage measurement under xdist must equal serial values (≥ fail_under = 70) and test outcomes must remain identical to serial runs."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785824273277643826,"uuid":"76948462-8572-4779-94e3-d72bde8aeb72"}